{"seq":469,"elapsed_ms":4624,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"We need answer exactly one complete DUT between [BEGIN] and [DONE], no explanation. Need fix bug. Specification: adder-subtractor with zero flag? Actually described module with always @(*) if without else latches. Need combinational complete assignments. For shut_off_computer: if cpu_overheated then 1 else presumably 0. keep_driving: if ~arrived then ~gas_tank_empty else 0? Need infer intended behavior. Original:\n\nalways @(*) begin\n if (cpu_overheated)\n    shut_off_computer = 1;\nend\n\nalways @(*) begin\n if (~arrived)\n    keep_driving = ~gas_tank_empty;\nend\n\nBug: missing else assignments creates latches. Fix: default assignment or else. What should defaults be? For shut_off_computer: If not overheated, leave computer on => shut_off_computer=0. For keep_driving: If arrived, don't keep driving => 0. If not arrived, keep_driving = ~gas_tank_empty. So:\n\nalways @(*) begin\n shut_off_computer = 1'b0;\n if (cpu_overheated) shut_off_computer = 1'b1;\nend\n\nalways @(*) begin\n keep_driving = 1'b0;\n if (~arrived) keep_driving = ~gas_tank_empty;\nend\n\nNeed deliver complete module. Use output reg as given. Could use ternary assign? Interface says output reg. Keep reg and always @*. Include ports.\n\nNeed ensure [BEGIN] [DONE]. No explanation.\n\nFinal with code."}}}
